.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt MBT_HTTP_CURL 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_http_curl_new ,
.Nm mbt_http_curl_free ,
.Nm mbt_http_curl_fn
.Nd Non-blocking HTTP client for tracker announces.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/http_curl.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_http_curl_new "struct mbt_http_curl **out" "struct mbt_ev *ev"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_http_curl_free "void *c"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_http_curl_fn "struct mbt_http_request *req" "mbt_http_done_fn done" \
"void *done_arg" "void *arg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions exist only in builds with libcurl.
They run HTTP and HTTPS requests on the event loop
.Fa ev ,
so a slow tracker does not stop peer traffic.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_http_curl_new
makes a client.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_http_curl_fn
is an
.Vt mbt_http_fn .
Pass the client as
.Fa arg .
.Pp
.Fn mbt_http_curl_free
frees the client.
Each pending request finishes as a failure before it returns.
.Pp
A request fails after 15 seconds, on an HTTP status of 400 or more, or when the
reply is over 8 MiB.
.Pp
A client serves one session.
Give it to the session with
.Fa http_free ,
so that
.Xr mbt_session_free 3
frees it first:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct mbt_http_curl *h;

mbt_http_curl_new(&h, ev);
cfg.http = mbt_http_curl_fn;
cfg.http_arg = h;
cfg.http_free = mbt_http_curl_free;
.Ed
.Pp
The session owns the client after
.Xr mbt_session_new 3
succeeds.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn mbt_http_curl_new
and
.Fn mbt_http_curl_fn
return 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt_session 3
.Sh CAVEATS
DNS lookups stop the loop if libcurl has no threaded or c-ares resolver.
